-- Code of Practice for General-Purpose AI Models, Safety and Security Chapter.
-- Baseline: the provider's questions about Commitment 9 (serious incident reporting).
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in EU law
-- has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: the provider of a general-purpose AI model, as a company deciding whether and
-- how the Code binds it. Every input is a fact the provider can state. The rules are
-- in cop-commitment-9.l4; this module only asks the questions and builds its records.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cop-domain`
IMPORT `cop-commitment-9`

§ `Does the Code bind me?`

@ref Recital (b), p. 3; Glossary 'model', p. 30
@export Does the Safety and Security Chapter of the EU Code of Practice for General-Purpose AI Models bind me as a provider? It binds only Signatories, and only for a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code of Practice for General-Purpose AI Models, Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories? (The Chapter does not say how a provider becomes a Signatory.)
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model in question a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act? The Chapter's word 'model' means only such a model.
GIVETH A `does the Chapter bind me`
`does this Code bind me` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` MEANS
    `whether the Chapter binds me` (`the provider's standing` WITH
        `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
        `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)

§ `Reporting a serious incident -- only once an incident has happened`

@ref Measure 9.3, first paragraph, pp. 26-27
@export By when must I make my initial report of a serious incident to the AI Office under Measure 9.3 of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter)? Gives the last day for each point that applies, counted in calendar days from the day you became aware of your model's involvement.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code's Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories?
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved in the incident a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act?
      `critical infrastructure` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure, and if so how is your model linked to it? One of: no such harm, or no link to my model; my model's involvement led to it, directly or indirectly; I establish or suspect with reasonable likelihood that my model caused it.
      `cybersecurity` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there a serious cybersecurity breach (the Code says this includes the (self-)exfiltration of model weights and cyberattacks), and if so how is your model linked to it? Same three choices.
      `death` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Did a person die, and if so how is your model linked to the death? Same three choices.
      `health` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there serious harm to a person's health, mental or physical, and if so how is your model linked to it? Same three choices.
      `fundamental rights` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there an infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights, and if so how is your model linked to it? Same three choices.
      `property` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there serious harm to property, and if so how is your model linked to it? Same three choices.
      `environment` IS A `my model's link to a harm` @desc Was there serious harm to the environment, and if so how is your model linked to it? Same three choices.
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become aware of your model's involvement in the incident (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-02)? The clock runs from this date, not from the incident.
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do exceptional circumstances apply? The Code makes its deadlines subject to 'exceptional circumstances' without defining them; if you say yes, no deadline is given.
GIVETH A `when my initial report is due`
`by when must I make my initial report` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` `critical infrastructure` `cybersecurity` `death` `health` `fundamental rights` `property` `environment` `the day I became aware` `exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `when my initial report is due under Measure 9.3`
        (`the provider's standing` WITH
            `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
            `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)
        (`the incident as I know it` WITH
            `link to a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure` IS `critical infrastructure`
            `link to a serious cybersecurity breach`                            IS `cybersecurity`
            `link to the death of a person`                                     IS `death`
            `link to serious harm to a person's health`                         IS `health`
            `link to an infringement of Union-law obligations that protect fundamental rights` IS `fundamental rights`
            `link to serious harm to property`                                  IS `property`
            `link to serious harm to the environment`                           IS `environment`
            `the date I became aware of my model's involvement in the incident` IS `the day I became aware`
            `exceptional circumstances apply`                                   IS `exceptional circumstances`)

@ref Measure 9.3, second paragraph, p. 27; Glossary 'resolved', p. 32
@export When is my next intermediate report on an unresolved serious incident due under Measure 9.3 of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter)? Intermediate reports are due at least every four weeks after the initial report until the incident is resolved.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code's Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories?
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved in the incident a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act?
      `my initial report was made on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you submit your initial report? Leave empty if you have not made one.
      `my latest intermediate report was made on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you submit your most recent intermediate report? Leave empty if you have made none.
      `the harm can be rectified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it possible to rectify the harm the incident caused?
      `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you adopt corrective measures to rectify the harm? Leave empty if you have not.
      `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you adopt corrective measures to assess and mitigate the systemic risks related to the incident? Leave empty if you have not.
GIVETH A `when my next intermediate report is due`
`when is my next intermediate report due` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` `my initial report was made on` `my latest intermediate report was made on` `the harm can be rectified` `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on` `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on` MEANS
    `when my next intermediate report is due under Measure 9.3`
        (`the provider's standing` WITH
            `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
            `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)
        `my initial report was made on`
        `my latest intermediate report was made on`
        (`my corrective measures` WITH
            `rectifying the harm is possible`                                   IS `the harm can be rectified`
            `the date I adopted corrective measures to rectify the harm`        IS `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on`
            `the date I adopted corrective measures to assess and mitigate the related systemic risks` IS `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on`)

@ref Measure 9.3, third paragraph, p. 27; Glossary 'resolved', p. 32
@export When is my final report on a serious incident due under Measure 9.3 of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter)? It is due not later than 60 days after the incident has been resolved.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code's Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories?
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved in the incident a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act?
      `the harm can be rectified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it possible to rectify the harm the incident caused?
      `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you adopt corrective measures to rectify the harm? Leave empty if you have not.
      `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did you adopt corrective measures to assess and mitigate the systemic risks related to the incident? Leave empty if you have not.
GIVETH A `when my final report is due`
`when is my final report due` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` `the harm can be rectified` `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on` `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on` MEANS
    `when my final report is due under Measure 9.3`
        (`the provider's standing` WITH
            `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
            `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)
        (`my corrective measures` WITH
            `rectifying the harm is possible`                                   IS `the harm can be rectified`
            `the date I adopted corrective measures to rectify the harm`        IS `I adopted measures to rectify the harm on`
            `the date I adopted corrective measures to assess and mitigate the related systemic risks` IS `I adopted measures on the related systemic risks on`)

@ref Measure 9.2 and Measure 9.3, first and third paragraphs, pp. 26-27
@export Does my initial or final serious-incident report give, or record as not yet held, every item of information Measure 9.2 and 9.3 of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter) require? An initial report needs items 1 to 7; a final report all nine.
GIVEN `which report` IS A `a report with fixed content` @desc Which report is this? One of: an initial report; a final report.
      `the items it gives` IS A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2` @desc Which items of Measure 9.2 does the report give? A list of: item 1, start and end dates; item 2, resulting harm and victims; item 3, chain of events; item 4, model involved; item 5, material on the model's involvement; item 6, what I intend to do or have done; item 7, what I recommend the authorities do; item 8, root cause analysis; item 9, patterns from post-market monitoring.
      `the items it records as not yet held` IS A LIST OF `an item of Measure 9.2` @desc Which items does the report record that you do not yet have? Same list of items.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`does my report give the required information` `which report` `the items it gives` `the items it records as not yet held` MEANS
    `the report accounts for every required item` (`the items the report must give` `which report`) `the items it gives` `the items it records as not yet held`

@ref Measure 9.3, fourth paragraph, p. 27
@export May I include a later, similar serious incident in the reports of the first one under Measure 9.3 of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter)? The Code does not define 'within the reporting timelines', so the answer is given on two readings.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code's Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories?
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act?
      `the later incident is similar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later serious incident similar to the first one?
      `the later incident occurred on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the later incident occur?
      `the first incident's initial report was due by` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day for the first incident's initial report?
      `the first incident's final report is due by` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc What is the last day for the first incident's final report? Leave empty if the first incident is not yet resolved.
GIVETH A `may I report a later similar incident with the first`
`may I report a similar incident with the first` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` `the later incident is similar` `the later incident occurred on` `the first incident's initial report was due by` `the first incident's final report is due by` MEANS
    `whether I may report a later similar incident with the first`
        (`the provider's standing` WITH
            `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
            `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)
        `the later incident is similar`
        `the later incident occurred on`
        `the first incident's initial report was due by`
        `the first incident's final report is due by`

§ `Keeping the documentation`

@ref Measure 9.4, p. 27
@export How long must I keep the documentation I gathered under Commitment 9 (serious incident reporting) of the EU GPAI Code of Practice (Safety and Security Chapter)? At least five years from the date of the documentation or of the incident, whichever is later; given on both readings of 'the date of the serious incident'.
GIVEN `am I a Signatory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you signed the Code's Safety and Security Chapter, so that you are one of its Signatories?
      `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the model involved a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk within the AI Act?
      `the documentation is dated` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of this piece of documentation?
      `the incident started on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the serious incident start (or your best approximation)?
      `the incident ended on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc On what date did the serious incident end (or your best approximation)? Leave empty if it lasted one day or has not ended.
GIVETH A `how long I must keep the documentation`
`how long must I keep the records` `am I a Signatory` `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk` `the documentation is dated` `the incident started on` `the incident ended on` MEANS
    `how long I must keep it under Measure 9.4`
        (`the provider's standing` WITH
            `I am a Signatory of the Chapter`                                   IS `am I a Signatory`
            `the model involved is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS `is my model a GPAI model with systemic risk`)
        `the documentation is dated`
        `the incident started on`
        `the incident ended on`
